text:
Race condition. Multiple requests read same value before any write commit.

## Fix: Atomic Update

```sql
-- Bad: read then write (race)
SELECT counter FROM table WHERE id = $1;
UPDATE table SET counter = $2 WHERE id = $1;

-- Good: atomic increment, returns new value
UPDATE table SET counter = counter + 1 WHERE id = $1
RETURNING counter;
```

One query. DB serialize writes. No gap for race.

## Node.js

```js
// Bad
const { rows: [row] } = await pool.query('SELECT counter FROM t WHERE id = $1', [id]);
await pool.query('UPDATE t SET counter = $2 WHERE id = $1', [row.counter + 1, id]);
res.json({ counter: row.counter + 1 }); // stale if concurrent

// Good
const { rows: [row] } = await pool.query(
  'UPDATE t SET counter = counter + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING counter',
  [id]
);
res.json({ counter: row.counter }); // always fresh
```

## If Need Complex Logic

Wrap in transaction + row lock:

```js
const client = await pool.connect();
try {
  await client.query('BEGIN');
  const { rows: [row] } = await client.query(
    'SELECT counter FROM t WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE', // locks row
    [id]
  );
  // do complex logic here
  const newVal = row.counter + 1;
  await client.query('UPDATE t SET counter = $1 WHERE id = $2', [newVal, id]);
  await client.query('COMMIT');
  res.json({ counter: newVal });
} catch (e) {
  await client.query('ROLLBACK');
  throw e;
} finally {
  client.release();
}
```

`FOR UPDATE` block other transactions until commit. Serialize access.

## Pick Right Fix

| Situation | Fix |
|-----------|-----|
| Simple increment | `UPDATE ... SET x = x + 1 RETURNING x` |
| Complex logic on value | Transaction + `FOR UPDATE` |
| High contention, can retry | Optimistic lock (version column + retry) |

Atomic update cover 90% cases.
